;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: default-menu.gc
;; name in dgo: default-menu
;; dgos: ENGINE, GAME

;; og:preserve-this landing (issue 571's UX successor, R3 of the debug-menu
;; scoping plan): transcribed from jakx's own clean scoped decode of this
;; object (13 decompiler ERROR markers going in; the race-selection rs3 fix
;; below resolves dm-play-race's enum error and its two data-label loads for
;; free, leaving 12). Hand-work landed on top of the transcription:
;;   - all-texture-tweak-adjust is stubbed to (none), matching jak3's own
;;     precedent (jak3 default-menu.gc:1013-1016) rather than the raw decode,
;;     which reads a literal PLACEHOLDER token off a dynamic-array-field-access
;;     that is not valid GOAL.
;;   - the 17 int shader-tweak fields (l, k, mmin, mmag, lcm, tfx, tbp, tbw,
;;     tw, th, mxl, wms, wmt, minu, maxu, minv, maxv) plus the float "tweak"
;;     field decode to bare label references (<lambda at LNNN>, not compiler-
;;     visible symbols) because the decompiler cannot fold the raw shader-walk
;;     pointer arithmetic into a lambda body; all 18 are hand-written verbatim
;;     from jak3's own landed twin (same function, same og:preserve-this shift
;;     amounts for k/tfx/minv/maxv), since gs-tex0/gs-tex1/gs-clamp carry an
;;     identical bit layout in this worktree's all-types.gc (hardware GS
;;     register format, unchanged across games).
;;   - four more bare-label lambdas resolve the same way: build-instance-list's
;;     four (sort ...) comparators (identical `(lambda ((arg0 debug-menu)
;;     (arg1 debug-menu)) (string<=? (-> arg0 name) (-> arg1 name)))` in jak3),
;;     debug-menu-make-camera-menu's "Edit" '*cam-layout* toggle (identical
;;     cam-layout-start/cam-layout-stop pair, both already landed in
;;     engine/camera/cam-layout.gc), and the Actor menu's "Traffic Start"/
;;     "Traffic Kill" (identical valid?-guarded traffic-start/traffic-kill
;;     function-var calls, both already carried as provisional call-site-only
;;     externs in all-types.gc).
;;   - dm-vu1-user-all-pick-func's raw offset-172 load/store of a static
;;     64-bit label (L6899, "Failed to guess label use") is resolved the same
;;     way: jak3's own twin uses the identical `(the-as uint #x...)` compare-
;;     and-set idiom against *display* vu1-enable-user-menu, but jak3's own
;;     literal (#x17fffffff8) is wrong for jakx (a different vu1-renderer-mask
;;     bit count per game); the landed value (#x5fffffff8) is read directly
;;     off this object's own two static words at L6899 in the fresh ir2.asm
;;     (.word 0xfffffff8, .word 0x5), not copied from jak3.
;;   - six bare-label lambdas are HELD rather than reconstructed because their
;;     one solid anchor, jak3's own twin, depends on *target*, a global symbol
;;     that does not exist anywhere in jakx (target-pos takes an explicit
;;     player index instead, "jak3-parity sig" per all-types.gc, a genuine
;;     split-screen API divergence): the Game menu's "Kill Target" and "Hit
;;     Target", and the Actor menu's "Save Continue". Three more have no jak3
;;     twin at all (jakx-only, racing-specific, zero recovered body): "Get All
;;     Vehicles Parts", "Get All Tasks", and "Trick Out Vehicles". All six
;;     stay inline no-op stubs with a per-site og:preserve-this note; pressing
;;     them in-game is a silent no-op rather than the retail behavior.
;;   - eight named functions fail decode entirely into register-soup
;;     (hundreds of local-vars, "Failed to guess stack use") rather than a
;;     resolvable bare label: dm-cam-settings-func, dm-cam-setting-float,
;;     dm-subdiv-int, dm-current-continue, build-shader-list,
;;     dm-split-screen-toggle-pick-func, dm-anim-tester-flag-func and
;;     dm-anim-tester-func. dm-subdiv-int's raw offset (276, off *anim-tester*)
;;     was checked against jak3's landed anim-tester type and does NOT match
;;     jak3's own "speed" field offset (232), so the type has grown between
;;     games and no jakx anim-tester deftype exists to name the field; the
;;     other seven were not chased further given the same "no landed twin
;;     offset/symbol to anchor a port" shape. All eight are held as
;;     type-correct trivial stubs (see each site) with a test/offline/config/
;;     jakx/config.jsonc skip_compile_functions entry, since the fresh
;;     re-decompile of each will always reproduce the same uncompilable raw
;;     form.
;;   - 32 further callback externs referenced by this file's menu templates
;;     have no defmethod/defun anywhere in goal_src (declared in all-types.gc
;;     only); they stay unlanded per the scoping table. The menu resolves them
;;     at press time, so each is a dead arm only if actually pressed, not a
;;     compile-time problem. Six of those arms are dead in retail itself, not
;;     merely unlanded here: bug-report-start/stop, loader-test-command,
;;     net-race-start/stop and spawn-hostile call into subsystems retail never
;;     wires live; not chased further.
;;   - race-selection gains an (rs3 3) entry (decompiler/config/jakx/all-
;;     types.gc and goal_src/jakx/engine/game/main-h.gc, same commit): the
;;     name follows this enum's own existing rs1 placeholder convention,
;;     since dm-play-race switches on this value with no recovered symbolic
;;     name either.
;;   - dm-play-task-with-continue was a ninth, distinct hold (the fresh
;;     decode did not convert it to expressions at all, no partial body of
;;     any kind): landed by the play-arm rung once play-task's own CFG-
;;     unrelated walls cleared showed the real blocker was a degenerate
;;     branch-to-fallthrough CFG failure, not a type-prop gap; see that
;;     function's own og:preserve-this note below for the config fix.
;;   - the "Nav Graph" submenu is a discovery beyond the scoping plan's own
;;     error tally: every item in it decodes clean (no ERROR marker at all),
;;     but it calls nav-graph-editor-method-N by number and depends on
;;     get-nav-graph-editor/run-nav-graph-editor/exit-nav-graph-editor, all
;;     three keyed on a nav-graph-editor type that has no deftype anywhere in
;;     this worktree's goal_src (all-types.gc carries it as a decompiler-side
;;     reference only). Landing that type and its ~66+ methods is a whole
;;     separate subsystem, out of this rung's scope; the entire submenu (was
;;     roughly 30 items) is held as one inert placeholder rather than landed
;;     item-by-item, and none of it counts against the 31 bare-label-lambda
;;     or 8 register-soup-function tallies above, since it was never a
;;     decompiler error to begin with. This also cost the three
;;     get-nav-graph-editor/run-nav-graph-editor/exit-nav-graph-editor
;;     forward externs their reason to exist, so they are not declared below
;;     either (their sole home was inside this now-held submenu).

;; this file is debug only
(declare-file (debug))

;; og:preserve-this forward externs: none of the following symbols have a
;; landed home anywhere else in goal_src (all-types.gc carries each only as
;; an extern, no defun/define/defstate, and no jak1/jak2/jak3 twin exists for
;; any of them to compare against, checked against a full scan of this
;; worktree's goal_src/jakx tree), so the compiler cannot resolve this file's
;; own call and value sites to them without a same-file declaration (same
;; class as debug.gc's own forward extern for draw-string, #174; all-types.gc
;; alone is not enough, since it feeds the decompiler and the
;; JakXTypeConsistency gtest, not the real build). All resolve at call or
;; deref time rather than at compile time. Six are dead in retail itself
;; (bug-report-start/stop, loader-test-command, net-race-start/stop,
;; spawn-hostile: their call sites reach subsystems retail never wires
;; live); traffic-start/traffic-kill back the "Traffic Start"/"Traffic Kill"
;; menu items landed below; editable-player-init and
;; nav-mesh-editor-init are the :init behaviors of two processes whose own
;; files build their -h/data but not yet that behavior; the rest back plain
;; menu-item callbacks, debug utilities or globals with no further chase
;; attempted.
(define-extern set-local-vehicle (function int none))
(define-extern bug-report-start (function object))
(define-extern bug-report-stop (function object))
(define-extern loader-test-command (function object object object))
(define-extern net-race-start (function object))
(define-extern net-race-stop (function object))
(define-extern spawn-hostile (function object))
;; typed (function none) here, not all-types.gc's own weaker "object" guess:
;; jak3's own twin declares both this exact way (decompiler/config/jak3/
;; all-types.gc), the (gp-0) call below needs a function-typed value to
;; type-check, and the valid?-guarded 0-arg-call usage is identical to jak3's.
(define-extern traffic-start (function none))
(define-extern traffic-kill (function none))
;; og:preserve-this type retire: object was this extern's provisional guess from
;; before net-start.gc landed; the real (define *net-start-view-ct* 1) there is
;; int, all-types agrees, and this file's own uses do int arithmetic on it.
(define-extern *net-start-view-ct* int)
(define-extern *shader-pick-menu* object)
(define-extern *stats-blerc* object)
(define-extern bug-report-display (function symbol int))
;; og:preserve-this forward declaration, retired from runtime hazard (entity
;; S-stage rung): debug-actor now has a real defun-debug in entity.gc (build
;; order 329), which compiles before this file (default-menu.o, 504), so the
;; symbol is already a real bound value by the time this declaration is
;; reached.
(define-extern debug-actor (function string none))
(define-extern debug-reset-prim-buffer (function none))
;; og:preserve-this forward-extern retire (play-arm rung): dm-play-task-with-
;; continue now has a landed home in this same file, just above dm-play-task
;; (its own body's original object-file position, and its only two callers).
(define-extern dm-set-veh-leco (function int none))
;; arg1 declared int here, not all-types.gc's own int32: goalc's typecheck
;; rejects a bare int literal, a (the-as int32 N) cast, and a (the int32 N)
;; cast alike against a formal int32 parameter ("got a 'int' when expecting
;; a 'int32'" every time); no expression built from an integer literal at a
;; call site reads back as int32 in this compiler, only a genuine int32
;; value already in hand does (e.g. a variable populated elsewhere, as
;; wvehicle-weapons-debug.gc's own landed defun does internally). All
;; thirteen call sites below pass literal weapon-id constants, so this
;; extern is declared int to match what they can actually produce; the
;; matching all-types.gc correction ripples into wvehicle-weapons-debug's
;; own REF (regenerated alongside this file's).
(define-extern dm-set-veh-weapon (function symbol int none))
(define-extern editable-player-init (function symbol none :behavior editable-player))
(define-extern start-drift (function none))
(define-extern end-end-credits (function none))
(define-extern merc-stats (function none))
(define-extern nav-mesh-editor-init (function symbol object :behavior nav-mesh-editor))
(define-extern play-clean (function symbol int))
(define-extern print-prototype-intersection-list (function object object))
(define-extern print-prototype-list (function none))
(define-extern prototype-bucket-recalc-fields (function prototype-bucket prototype-bucket))
(define-extern prototype-bucket-type (function prototype-bucket type))
(define-extern read-sound-info-tweaks (function none))
(define-extern spartacus-start (function none))
(define-extern spartacus-stop (function none))
(define-extern task-node-close! (function game-task-node symbol int))
(define-extern task-node-closed? (function game-task-node symbol))
(define-extern task-node-open? (function game-task-node symbol))

;; og:preserve-this debug-segment guard (runtime-falsified, tip smoke): same
;; class as editable-player.gc's own *editable-menu-context* guard (see that
;; file's og:preserve-this note for the full C++ citation) - the 'debug
;; kheap this constructor allocates its font sub-object on only exists when
;; booted with -debug (game/kernel/jakx/kmachine.cpp:296-302), and
;; *debug-segment* itself reads back the identical flag
;; (game/kernel/jakx/kscheme.cpp:1924-1929), so it is the correct guard, not
;; a redundant one. *menu-hook* below is patched to match, since it
;; dereferences this context every frame regardless of debug-segment.
;;
;; definition for symbol *debug-menu-context*, type debug-menu-context
(define *debug-menu-context* (when *debug-segment* (new 'debug 'debug-menu-context)))

;; definition for symbol *dm-cam-mode-interpolation*, type object
(define *dm-cam-mode-interpolation* (the-as object 0))

;; definition for function dm-cam-mode-func
(defun dm-cam-mode-func ((arg0 (state camera-slave)) (arg1 debug-menu-msg))
  (if (and (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press)) arg0)
      (setting-control-method-22 *setting-control* 'mode-name (-> arg0 name) 0 0)
      )
  (if (view-get-active-camera)
      (send-event (view-get-active-camera) 'query-state arg0)
      (not arg0)
      )
  )

;; definition for function dm-cam-mode-default
(defun dm-cam-mode-default ((arg0 object) (arg1 debug-menu-msg))
  (if (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press))
      (setting-control-method-21 *setting-control* 'mode-name)
      )
  (not (setting-control-method-20 *setting-control* 'mode-name))
  )

;; definition for function dm-cam-settings-default
(defun dm-cam-settings-default ((arg0 object) (arg1 debug-menu-msg))
  (when (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press))
    (setting-control-method-21 *setting-control* 'fov)
    (setting-control-method-21 *setting-control* 'slave-options)
    )
  (and (not (setting-control-method-20 *setting-control* 'fov))
       (not (setting-control-method-20 *setting-control* 'slave-options))
       )
  )

;; og:preserve-this held (register-soup decode): the fresh decode fails to
;; convert this function to expressions ("failed type prop at 246: Could not
;; figure out load: (set! v1 (l.wu (+ v0 156)))", "Failed to guess stack use
;; for 16"), leaving a 550-line raw register dump (v0-0 through v0-34,
;; dozens of process/object-typed locals) rather than a resolvable bare
;; label. No landed jakx twin offset or symbol anchors a port. Held as a
;; type-correct stub (see test/offline/config/jakx/config.jsonc
;; skip_compile_functions for the matching raw-decode compile skip); the
;; camera-settings toggle menu items that call it become no-ops.
(defun dm-cam-settings-func ((arg0 int) (arg1 debug-menu-msg))
  #f
  )

;; definition for function dm-cam-settings-func-int
;; WARN: Return type mismatch object vs int.
(defun dm-cam-settings-func-int ((arg0 int) (arg1 debug-menu-msg) (arg2 int) (arg3 int))
  (view-push-context 0)
  (when (and (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press)) (view-get-active-camera))
    (if (= (/ arg0 8) 5)
        (set! *dm-cam-mode-interpolation* arg2)
        )
    )
  (set! arg3 (cond
               ((view-get-active-camera)
                (cond
                  ((= (/ arg0 8) 5)
                   (the-as int *dm-cam-mode-interpolation*)
                   )
                  (else
                    (empty)
                    arg3
                    )
                  )
                )
               (else
                 (empty)
                 arg3
                 )
               )
        )
  (view-pop-context)
  (the-as int arg3)
  )

;; definition for function dm-cam-externalize
(defun dm-cam-externalize ((arg0 symbol) (arg1 debug-menu-msg))
  (when (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press))
    (cond
      ((= arg0 'reset)
       (if (!= *external-cam-mode* 'locked)
           (external-cam-reset!)
           )
       )
      ((= arg0 'allow-z)
       (set! *external-cam-options* (logxor *external-cam-options* (external-cam-option allow-z)))
       )
      ((= *external-cam-mode* arg0)
       (set! *external-cam-mode* #f)
       )
      (else
        (if (not *external-cam-mode*)
            (external-cam-reset!)
            )
        (set! *external-cam-mode* arg0)
        )
      )
    )
  (if (= arg0 'allow-z)
      (logtest? *external-cam-options* (external-cam-option allow-z))
      (= *external-cam-mode* arg0)
      )
  )

;; og:preserve-this held (register-soup decode): the fresh decode fails to
;; convert this function to expressions ("failed type prop at 51: Could not
;; figure out load: (set! v1 (l.wu (+ v0 148)))"), leaving a raw register
;; dump (a "connection"-typed local among others) rather than a resolvable
;; bare label. No landed jakx twin offset or symbol anchors a port. Held as a
;; type-correct stub returning the caller's own fallback value (see
;; test/offline/config/jakx/config.jsonc skip_compile_functions for the
;; matching raw-decode compile skip); the fov-setting menu item that calls it
;; reports its fallback rather than the retail behavior.
(defun dm-cam-setting-float ((arg0 float) (arg1 debug-menu-msg) (arg2 float) (arg3 float))
  arg3
  )

;; definition for function dm-cam-render-float
(defun dm-cam-render-float ((arg0 int) (arg1 debug-menu-msg) (arg2 float) (arg3 float))
  (view-push-context 0)
  (when (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press))
    (when (zero? (/ arg0 8))
      (when (view-get-active-math-camera)
        (set! (-> (view-get-active-math-camera) fov) (* 182.04445 arg2))
        (update-math-camera
          (view-get-active-math-camera)
          (-> *setting-control* user-current video-mode)
          (-> *setting-control* user-current aspect-ratio)
          (-> (view-get-active-math-camera) fov)
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (set! arg3 (cond
               ((zero? (/ arg0 8))
                (cond
                  ((view-get-active-math-camera)
                   (* 0.005493164 (-> (view-get-active-math-camera) fov))
                   )
                  (else
                    (empty)
                    arg3
                    )
                  )
                )
               (else
                 (empty)
                 arg3
                 )
               )
        )
  (let ((f30-2 arg3))
    (view-pop-context)
    f30-2
    )
  )

;; definition for function dm-subdiv-float
(defun dm-subdiv-float ((arg0 symbol) (arg1 debug-menu-msg) (arg2 float) (arg3 float))
  (view-push-context 0)
  (when (= arg1 (debug-menu-msg press))
    (case arg0
      (('close)
       (when (and (view-get-active-math-camera) *subdivide-settings*)
         (dotimes (v1-5 20)
           (set! (-> *subdivide-settings* close v1-5) (* 4096.0 arg2))
           )
         )
       )
      (('far)
       (when (and (view-get-active-math-camera) *subdivide-settings*)
         (dotimes (v1-11 20)
           (set! (-> *subdivide-settings* far v1-11) (* 4096.0 arg2))
           )
         )
       )
      )
    )
  (set! arg3 (cond
               ((= arg0 'close)
                (cond
                  ((and (view-get-active-math-camera) *subdivide-settings*)
                   (/ (-> *subdivide-settings* close 0) METER_LENGTH)
                   )
                  (else
                    (empty)
                    arg3
                    )
                  )
                )
               ((= arg0 'far)
                (cond
                  ((and (view-get-active-math-camera) *subdivide-settings*)
                   (/ (-> *subdivide-settings* far 0) METER_LENGTH)
                   )
                  (else
                    (empty)
                    arg3
                    )
                  )
                )
               (else
                 (empty)
                 arg3
                 )
               )
        )
  (let ((f30-0 arg3))
    (view-pop-context)
    f30-0
    )
  )

;; og:preserve-this held (register-soup decode): the fresh decode fails to
;; convert this function to expressions ("failed type prop at 8: Could not
;; figure out load: (set! v1 (l.wu v1))"). jak3's own landed twin reads/
;; writes `(-> *anim-tester* 0 speed)` at offset 232 of its anim-tester type;
;; jakx's raw decode instead reads/writes offset 276 of the same dereferenced
;; pointer, so the type has grown between games, and no jakx anim-tester
